-- ============================================================================
-- Carry the old Google "SPEEKS Company Calendar" into store_calendar_events.
-- APPLIED 2026-10-01 through the Supabase MCP (execute_sql). This file is the
-- provenance record; the rows are tagged source = 'google', so re-running it is
--   delete from store_calendar_events where source = 'google';  then this.
--
-- Source: Ethan's .ics export, 2026-10-01, 108 events. The two repeating Google
-- events were expanded and their edited instances kept as edited
-- ("WSP and Partial OVL Pickup", "OVL Recycle Vendor Pickup"), giving 109 rows.
-- Times are converted from UTC to Central; all-day end dates made inclusive.
--
-- Google's colours carried no fixed meaning (Ethan: "that's what I want you to
-- do"), and an .ics export doesn't include them anyway. They are replaced by
-- `category`, which the calendar draws as a colour dot. The rules used:
--   * a store code / Maplewood / Ballwin in the title  -> that store only
--   * birthdays, work anniversaries, first days, PTO    -> the person's store
--     from users (CORP people -> all stores). Current staff's birthdays and
--     anniversaries repeat yearly; anniversaries are retitled
--     "X's work anniversary" with "Started YYYY." in notes, since "1-Year!"
--     would be wrong the following year. People not on the roster are kept as
--     one-off history, not repeated.
--   * "Ethan in STL ..."                 -> MPL + BAL, category travel
--   * pay days, Labor/Columbus Day, PayMore promos, the manager meeting and
--     training                           -> all stores
--   * community events (chambers, e-waste, Nerdcon, LSR7) -> the stores in
--     that area (KC = OVL/LEE/WSP, STL = MPL/BAL)
--   * B2B / recycle pickups with no store named -> the three KC stores
--   * "Dri Design", "Dynamic Logistix" kept as written, category other.
-- Shown to Ethan in full before and after; md5 of the rows matched the
-- generated list (b71699ff556c5897080eced50f319b10).
-- ============================================================================

